<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Comalco falls into loss for 96 year.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Comalco falls into loss for 96 year.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 17.4 vs 295.0</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		3.0 vs 13.00</p>
<p>NOTE: Comalco Ltd is a bauxite miner and alumina and aluminium producer and is about 67 percent owned by RTZ Corp CRA Ltd group. Net profit is on a statutory accounting basis.  </p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			1.64 vs 2.17</p>
<p>    Other income			   67.1 vs 91.1</p>
<p>    Abnormal items (gross)     loss 115.0 vs profit 18.9</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			 nil vs loss 42.0</p>
<p>    Tax					61.1 vs 113.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Comalco said operating profit before abnormals and superannuation adjustment but after tax and outside equity interest was A$32.9 million against A$264.8 million in 1995. Operating profit and extraordinary items after tax was a loss of A$16.8 million compared with a profit of A$232.3 million a year earlier.  </p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		   loss    3.1 vs 48.9</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		6.0 vs 25.0</p>
<p>Dividend is nil franked</p>
<p>Pay date March 25</p>
<p>Reg date March 11</p>
<p>    Interest				 56.3 vs  41.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  114.7 vs 111.7</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil vs credit 1.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Comalco said the abnormal loss reflected closure of its kaolin business and costs associated with sale of Australian and New Zealand downstream operations and restructuring costs.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
